          %h2#references References
          %p
            The site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FormalCartSp"} FormalCartSp
            is discussed in section 5 of
          %ul
            %li#Kock86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
              ,
              %em Convenient vector spaces embed into the Cahiers topos
              , Cahiers de Topologie et Géométrie Différentielle Catégoriques, 27 no. 1 (1986), p. 3-17 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1986__27_1_3_0"}> numdam
              ).
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers+topos"} Cahiers topos
          %p
            The notion of formally étale maps as obtained here from the general abstract definition in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            coincided on 0-truncated objects with that defined on p. 82 of
          %ul
            %li#Kock81
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
              ,
              %em Synthetic Differential Geometry
              (1981) (
              %a{:href => "http://home.imf.au.dk/kock/sdg99.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#StrucPaths"} infinitesimal path ∞-groupoid adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Red
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mi inf
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi inf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{Red} \dashv \mathbf{\Pi}_{inf} \dashv \mathbf{\flat}_{inf})
            and the de Rham theorem for
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            in section 3 of
          %ul
            %li#SimpsonTeleman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                deRham theorem for
                = succeed "-stacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~teleman/math/simpson.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SynthDiff
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SynthDiff\infty Grpd
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                , section 4.4 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Proper+Orbifold+Cohomology"} Proper Orbifold Cohomology
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.01101"}> arXiv:2008.01101
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Introduction+to+Higher+Supergeometry"} Introduction to Higher Supergeometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Structures+in+M-Theory+2018"} Higher Structures in M-Theory 2018
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/"} Durham Symposium
              %p
                published in parts as:
                %em Higher Structures in M-Theory
                (with
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jur%C4%8Do"} Branislav Jurčo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"} Christian Saemann
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Wolf"} Martin Wolf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02807"} arXiv:1903.02807
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201910001"} doi:10.1002/prop.201910001
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+localization"} cohomology localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SynthDiff
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SynthDiff\infty Grpd
            and the infinitesimal singular simplicial complex as a presentation for infinitesimal paths objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SynthDiff
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SynthDiff\infty Grpd
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Stel
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Stel"}> Herman Stel
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-Stacks and their function algebras – with applications to
                = succeed "-Lie" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              , master thesis (2010) (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Stel"}> web
              )
          %p
            The discussion of the cohomology localization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SynthDiff
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SynthDiff\infty Grpd
            follows that in another context in
          %ul
            %li#Toen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Champs affines
              %strong 12
              (2006), no. 1, 39-135 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0012219"}> arXiv:math/0012219
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00029-006-0019-z"} doi:10.1007/s00029-006-0019-z
          %p
            The construction of the infinitesimal path object has been amplified and discussed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"} Anders Kock
            under the name
            = succeed "," do
              %em combinatorial differential forms
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
              ,
              %em Synthetic Geometry of Manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://home.imf.au.dk/kock/SGM-final.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The discussion that the normalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+algebra"} cosimplicial algebra
            of functions on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+singular+simplicial+complex"} infinitesimal singular simplicial complex
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            is further discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Herman Stel,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cosimplicial+C-infinity+rings+and+the+de+Rham+complex+of+Euclidean+space"} Cosimplicial C-infinity rings and the de Rham complex of Euclidean space
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/arXiv:1310.7407"}> arXiv:arXiv:1310.7407
              )
          %p
            The results on differentiable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group+cohomology"} Lie group cohomology
            used above is in
          %ul
            %li#Blanc
              P. Blanc,
              %em Cohomologie différentiable et changement de groupes
              Astérisque, vol. 124-125 (1985), pp. 113-130.
          %p recalled in
          %ul
            %li#Brylinski
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              %em Differentiable Cohomology of Gauge Groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0011069"}> arXiv
              )
          %p which parallels
          %ul
            %li#Segal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              %em Cohomology of topological groups
              , Symposia Mathematica, Vol IV (1970) (1986?) p. 377
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-site" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Formal+moduli+problems"} Formal moduli problems
          %p following
          %ul
            %li#Hinich
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em DG coalgebras as formal stacks
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9812034"} arXiv:math/9812034
